.TH GIT-EZ 1 "" "git-ez" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-ez \- AI-assisted native Git integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git ez
.RI "rebase|merge|cherry-pick target " [ options ]
.br
.B git ez
.RI "rebase|merge|cherry-pick --continue " [ options ]
.br
.B git ez
.RI "audit list|show " [ options ]
.br
.B git ez probe
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Git-ez delegates integration operations to native Git. When an eligible textual
conflict needs assistance, an agent investigates the repository and proposes
edits. Git-ez verifies the proposal, performs configured validation and controls
staging and native continuation.
.PP
Use
.B git-ez --help
or
.B git-ez COMMAND --help
for the complete option list supplied by the installed executable.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --repo " directory"
Select the repository. Filesystem symbolic links and parent components retain
native path semantics.
.TP
.B --interactive
Review the complete proposal before accepting it. Reject with feedback to request
a revision, or quit to restore the original tracked conflict state.
.TP
.BI --check " command arguments..."
Validate with literal command arguments. Place this option last; the remaining
arguments belong to the validation command.
.TP
.B --continue
Continue an existing native operation. Assistance eligibility follows the current
Git operation state; unrelated native failures remain manual recovery tasks.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Use native Git configuration under
.BR ez.* .
Set
.B ez.model
and configure the provider and endpoint as required. Supported protocols are
OpenAI-compatible and native Ollama. Consult the distributed
.B docs/configuration.md
for keys, defaults, credentials and TLS configuration.
.SH AUDIT
.B git ez audit list
lists saved AI interventions.
.B git ez audit show
inspects a saved run; use command help for verbose, artifact and session options.
Consultation is offline and does not require provider credentials.
Model-free operations do not create persistent LLM audit runs.
.SH SAFETY
Git remains responsible for operation state and recovery. Inspect the reported
failure and native Git status before continuing or aborting an interrupted
operation. Agent command controls do not constitute an operating-system sandbox.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Git 2.46 or later on a supported Linux, FreeBSD or macOS system.
The standalone executable does not require Python or an installed manual.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-merge (1),
.BR git-rebase (1),
.BR git-cherry-pick (1)
